From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 01:31:56 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 423/488] [DS4.1] Drop the target's unread MTP hidden-state
 buffer

With any hidden-state drafter (DSpark included), the target allocated
_mtp_hidden_buffer, max_num_batched_tokens rows of the four residual
streams (hc_dim, BF16: 671 MB at 16384 tokens), and copied every
forward's streams into it outside sequence-parallel prefill (3.9 MB a
c16 decode step, up to 655 MB a 16K prefill chunk). No DS4.1 model
defines get_mtp_target_hidden_states, so nothing reads it: the runner
hands the drafter the collapsed states. The buffer, its copy and the
prefill gather of the full streams it forced go; the collapse and norm
stay per row, so outputs are unchanged.
